Bugfix: Add `utc-node-times` feature flag for timezone-independent tree deduplication

Node timestamps were stored in trees with the local timezone offset of the
machine running the backup. Backing up unchanged files with a different
`TZ` produced different tree blobs, so every directory was stored again and
the `Dirs: changed` count spiked even though nothing had changed.

With the new alpha feature flag `utc-node-times` (for example
`RESTIC_FEATURES=utc-node-times=true`), node timestamps are normalized to UTC
before they enter a tree, making tree blobs identical across timezones.
Enabling the flag re-stores the tree blobs once; file content is not
re-uploaded.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22014
